<item name='HelpEHelpText'><richtext>
<pardef id='1' leftmargin='0.8125in' rightmargin='62%'/>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Exporting a View to Lotus-123 or to Excel</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Any view can be exported to a spreadsheet.  ne item to note, however, is that the data will be exported WYSIWYG (What You See Is What You Get).  so if some rows are hidden or collapsed, they will not be exported.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Also, many views use the Categorized Sort option - this looks prettier on the screen, but may make your export harder to manipulate for futher sorting etc.  </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
