</gif></picture><run
><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>If you want to remove the Categorized Sort, you will need to Edit your Private View; if the view you want to export is a public view, you will need to create a Private view, usin the Public View as the template.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>1. Launch the View that you want to export.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>2. On the top menu, select File, then Export</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>3. Select a location for the file, type in a filename, including the extension.  The fielanem should therefore resemble *.123.  Do not omit the extension - Notes won't do it for you.  Then select filetype Lotus 123 and click ok</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>4. A dialog box will prompt you to choose All Documents.  Remember to select the "Include View Titles".  Press ok and it is done.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>5. If you prefer an excel file, do all of the steps then launch Excel and copy/paste the DATA into Excel.  Do not copy/paste the columns/rows themselves, this won't work.  Just select the cells themselves.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par></richtext></item>
<item name='HelpFHelpText'><richtext>
<pardef id='2' leftmargin='0.8125in' rightmargin='62%'/>
<par def='2'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par></richtext></item>
<item name='HelpESubject'><text>Exporting a View</text></item>
<item name='HelpFSubject'><text>to translate</text></item></document>

